# Coding Standards

## Permission gate
No app implementation until the user explicitly allows coding (see `agent-workflow.mdc`).

## Structure
- Prefer modular code; do not artificially shrink a feature — write as much as the feature needs.
- Related UI for one feature goes in a **dedicated folder**, not scattered files.
- Prefer **reusable widgets** for buttons, cards, inputs, skeletons when the pattern repeats.
- Keep **logic separate from design/UI**.

## Design & data
- Design for **farmer UX**, not for DB/API schema.
- Follow `docs/context/UI_THEME.md` (colors, Literata / Nunito Sans, alignment).
- Think ahead: do not ship code you already know will be thrown away next step.
- During development: **no silent default fallbacks**. Fail visibly.

## Comments
- **Every Dart file** starts with an **explanatory** `///` file-purpose header + `library;` (where it sits in the app, what it is for). See `dart-file-headers.mdc` — not thin one-liners.
- Short comment on each function or feature you add so intent is clear later.

## Suggestions
- Suggest improvements that make the app clearer, more maintainable, or better for farmers (including UI and approach).
